
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-           inflateTT - Yet Another RFC-1951 Decompressor             -
-                 Written by Ville Helin in 2007                      -
-----------------------------------------------------------------------


1. DESCRIPTION

inflateTT is a command-line decompressor for DEFc files written by
deflateTT. It is a file-I/O wrapper around inflateTT-MP. See the
repository README for the bitstream, which is not a zlib stream.

The motivation behind writing this tool was to get a simple and
efficient data compression utility that didn't depend on any libraries,
like the pretty big and messy zlib, to my Nintendo DS homebrew projects.
deflateTT is the compression tool that outputs files that can be
decompressed using inflateTT.

Nintendo DS projects compile inflateTT-MP/inflate_ds.c. That file is the
16-bit entry point and keeps its own context.


2. CONTACT

If you have any questions, feel free to contact me at
vhelin#iki.fi.


3. VERSION HISTORY

v2.0 (10-Nov-2026)
  * Uses inflateTT-MP. Truncated, oversized and inconsistent input
    returns an error instead of walking off a buffer.
  * The test program is tests.exe in the repository root.

v1.2 (06-May-2007)
  * Added support for deflateTT v1.2 (DEFc) files.

v1.1 (21-Apr-2007)
  * The Huffman codes aren't read from the compressed files,
    but generated from the code lengths making this more
    RFC-1951 compatible.
  * The code lengths are now RLE+Huffman compressed, like
    RFC-1951 says.

v1.0 (27-Jan-2007)
  * The first public release


